#---
# purpose: "a self-send copies its message into a gift, as a send to another process does, so the sender's list stays intact and the copy is counted as the sender's allocation"
#---
#
# The program runs the same alias-and-rewrite shape twice. `retail` takes a
# list, keeps its head and replaces its tail with `[9]`; that one-cons
# construction holds Rewrite permission over the cell it was given, so when the
# cell is unaliased the runtime rewrites it in place.
#
# The control builds `kept_alias` from the head and tail of `kept`, which makes
# it the very cell `kept` starts with, and passes it to `retail`. Nothing else
# names that cell afterwards, so the rewrite happens in place: list retention
# telemetry counts it as a hit.
#
# The sent case builds `ys` the same way from `xs`, sends `xs` to self, then
# passes `ys` to `retail`. The send copies the three cells of `xs` into a gift
# that waits in the sender's mailbox, so the `list_cons_allocs` delta across
# the send is 3, and the mailbox holds no cell that `ys` or `xs` holds. The
# message is `[4, 5, 6]` when received. The rewrite of `ys` is still refused,
# because the compiler's call-site ownership rule
# (`construct_call_ownership` in src/compiler2/jobs/body.rs) marks the send
# argument Share, since the continuation retains `ys` and `ys` may alias it,
# and the Share mode publishes the list spine before the call. The rewrite
# finds the cell aliased and allocates a fresh one, which telemetry counts as a
# retention attempt without a hit.
#
# Across the run: four retention attempts, three hits. The missing hit is the
# refused rewrite of the sent cell.
def main() do
  kept = [1, 2, 3]
  [kh | kt] = kept
  kept_alias = [kh | kt]
  dbg(retail(kept_alias))

  xs = [4, 5, 6]
  [h | t] = xs
  ys = [h | t]
  before = System.alloc_stats()
  send(self(), xs)
  after_send = System.alloc_stats()
  dbg(after_send[:list_cons_allocs] - before[:list_cons_allocs])
  zs = retail(ys)
  receive do
    msg -> dbg(msg)
  end
  dbg(zs)
end

def retail(xs) do
  [h | _] = xs
  [h | [9]]
end
